  "verified_at": "2026-10-10",
  "baseline_note": "Mechanisms reviewed against the linked primary sources. Original synthetic data, algebraic derivations, SVG illustrations and Mermaid flow diagrams; numerical curves computed by the accompanying Python standard-library scripts. The local single-parameter perturbation, all seven hand-example gradients, simultaneous parameter update and subsequent forward/loss values were checked. Finite-difference gradients and deterministic full-batch training were executed. The intuitive explanations and derivations describe the same original example, not an additional source or experiment task. Framework source baselines are evidence references, not an installed or tested PyTorch dependency combination. The PyTorch comparison snippet was not executed. No real dataset, hardware, model benchmark or deployed runtime is validated. Dynamic web dates are the displayed last-updated dates; no web-page mirror is stored.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "tiny-network-001",
      "section": "1 为什么需要非线性激活",
      "statement": "Nonlinear activation changes the functions representable by stacked affine layers; ReLU is max(0,z).",
      "source_ids": [
        "google-neural-activation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "tiny-network-002",
      "section": "2 两个隐藏节点有哪些参数",
      "statement": "Learned weights and biases, Linear weight layout and batch shapes; seven-parameter count follows the original 1-2-1 structure.",
      "source_ids": [
        "pytorch-buildmodel-tutorial",
        "pytorch-linear-layer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "tiny-network-003",
      "section": "3 手算一次前向传播",
      "statement": "Forward evaluation composes affine operations, ReLU and the explicitly defined regression loss.",
      "source_ids": [
        "pytorch-buildmodel-tutorial",
        "pytorch-mse-loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "tiny-network-004",
      "section": "4 手算一次反向传播",
      "statement": "Backpropagation applies the chain rule and computes gradients without updating parameters; local gradient interpretation and inactive-branch behavior follow the original mathematical example. ReLU uses zero backward value at the threshold on the pinned CPU path.",
      "source_ids": [
        "pytorch-autograd-tutorial",
        "pytorch-relu-derivative",
        "pytorch-threshold-backward",
        "pytorch-cpu-threshold-kernel"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "tiny-network-005",
      "section": "5 从一个样本走到训练循环",
      "statement": "Forward evaluation, backward gradient computation and optimizer updates have separate roles; gradients are recomputed from current parameters and samples, with explicit clearing or accumulation. Training/evaluation mode and disabled gradient recording have distinct purposes.",
      "source_ids": [
        "pytorch-autograd-tutorial",
        "pytorch-optimization-tutorial"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "tiny-network-006",
      "section": "5 从一个样本走到训练循环",
      "statement": "MSELoss averages all output elements; half-MSE matches the article for one scalar output per sample.",
      "source_ids": [
        "pytorch-mse-loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "tiny-network-007",
      "section": "5 从一个样本走到训练循环",
      "statement": "Batch size, updates and epochs have distinct roles.",
      "source_ids": [
        "google-linear-hyperparameters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "tiny-network-008",
      "section": "6 运行两个节点的训练实验",
      "statement": "Synthetic training fit and a few constructed unseen inputs do not establish real-task generalization.",
      "source_ids": [
        "google-dataset-split"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "tiny-network-009",
      "section": "7 常见卡点与自测",
      "statement": "Activation conditions and input/target shape agreement are part of interpreting numerical loss and gradients.",
      "source_ids": [
        "google-neural-activation",
        "pytorch-mse-loss"
      ]
    }
  ],
